<mxCell id="n27" value="V6-36 (own TLS identities) -&amp;gt; V6-31 (non-root): the dependency the first plan missed" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=3;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.4;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontColor=#b85450;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n5" target="n8"><mxGeometry x="0" relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="430" y="480"/><mxPoint x="956" y="480"/></Array><mxPoint x="0" y="12" as="offset"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
<mxCell id="n28" value="The first plan's release shape put Phase 1 and Phase 2 in 6.0.0 and identity in 6.1. What shipped as 6.0.0 was identity (V6-01, V6-21, V6-30), done larger than recommended, with Phases 1 and 2 untouched: the Critical (V6-07) and ten Highs shipped unchanged under the major version. 6.1.0 should be Phase 1 and Phase 2, which now also carry TLS for the retail database (V6-52, V6-53) and the secure default in the code (V6-54); the acceptance tier (V6-67) should be in place before it is published." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fontColor=#555555;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="600" width="1480" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
